  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="41bb-d5d3-5530-ac22" name="Hibernians (Shieldwall) - List Notes" publicationId="af20-e256-4a51-93aa" hidden="false">
      <description>HIBERNIAN ARMY LISTS (Shieldwall, pp.56-64): Munster, Leinster, Connacht and Ulster. Percentages are by points. Special rules p.61 (Ambush: before units are placed, a Hibernian commander may keep one unit off the battlefield, written down as hidden; it is deployed when an enemy unit comes within 8" or earlier if he wishes, and is immune to psychology tests while hidden).
The Fianna are not part of the Common or Uncommon percentages (printed lists name only Bonnachts, Kerns, Madadh and Dogs of War).

ARMY COMPOSITIONS (pick one in the Army composition list):
[Munster]
  Characters: up to 33%
  Common Warriors: at least 50%
  Uncommon Warriors: up to 33%
  Munster (p.60). Characters up to 33%; Bonnachts and Kerns at least 50%; Madadh and Dogs of War (Vikings, Amsaigh, Gall-Gaedhil) up to 33%. The Fianna may have light armour (+3 pts). They may exchange javelins for thrusting spears (+3 pts); if armed with thrusting spear they may use Shieldwall.
[Leinster]
  Characters: up to 33%
  Common Warriors: up to 50%
  Uncommon Warriors: up to 33%
  Leinster (p.60). Characters up to 33%; Bonnachts and Kerns up to 50%; Madadh and Dogs of War (Vikings, Gestir, Amsaigh) up to 33%. The Fianna may have light armour (+3 pts). They may have throwing spears (+2 pts).
[Connacht]
  Characters: up to 33%
  Common Warriors: at least 50%
  Uncommon Warriors: up to 33%
  Connacht (p.60). Characters up to 33%; Bonnachts and Kerns at least 50%; Madadh and Dogs of War (Vikings, Amsaigh) up to 33%. The Fianna and Bonnachts count as light infantry.
[Ulster]
  Characters: up to 33%
  Common Warriors: up to 50%
  Uncommon Warriors: up to 33%
  Ulster (p.60). Characters up to 33%; Bonnachts and Kerns up to 50%; Madadh and Dogs of War (Vikings, Amsaigh, Gasraidh, Gall-Gaedhil) up to 33%. The Fianna may have light armour (+3 pts) and be Stubborn (+3 pts).</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
